@startuml fig-2-3-3-seq-dropoff-commit-swap
' SDS Figure II-2.3.3 — Drop-off commit at the zone gate, with slot swap
' New 2026-08-17. Level-triggered loop: it reads the live vehicle position and
' turns a provisional reservation into a binding commitment. At an entry point
' the winner may take a slot another cargo had only reserved; the displaced
' cargo is re-reserved and its TO3 re-aimed.
' Verified against wes/src/cargo/{dropoff-commit.loop,slot-reservation.service,
' dropoff-order.service}.ts.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng fig-2-3-3-seq-dropoff-commit-swap.puml
!include _style.iuml

participant DropoffCommitLoop as Loop
participant VehicleStateStore as Store
participant DeliverySlotEngine as Slots
participant SlotReservationService as Reserve
participant DropoffOrderService as Orders
participant "KernelApiService\n(ACL -> kernel)" as ACL
database PostgreSQL

Loop -> PostgreSQL: at start-up: pg_try_advisory_lock(815004711)
note right of Loop
  One instance only. A process that does not win the lock
  stays idle, so two schedulers never commit the same zone.
end note

loop every 500 ms (re-entrancy guarded by `ticking`)
  Loop -> PostgreSQL: SELECT tasks WHERE status = DELIVERING AND cargo_id IS NOT NULL
  Loop -> Store: get(assignedVehicleName)
  Store --> Loop: currentPosition | null
  Loop -> PostgreSQL: load cargo (ACTIVE, destination_location_name IS NULL)
  Loop -> Slots: layoutFor(destination zone)
  Slots --> Loop: ZoneSlotLayout

  alt position is one of layout.entryPoints
    Loop -> Reserve: commit(cargoId, zone, allowSwap = true)
  else position is a member point of the zone
    Loop -> Reserve: commit(cargoId, zone, allowSwap = false)
  else anywhere else
    Loop -> Loop: nothing to do — re-check on the next tick
  end

  Reserve -> PostgreSQL: BEGIN + pg_advisory_xact_lock(hashtext(zone.id))
  Reserve -> Slots: rank(layout, committed slots) - BR-11
  Slots --> Reserve: free slots in fill order
  alt allowSwap
    Reserve -> Reserve: chosen = best slot the ranking offers
  else
    Reserve -> Reserve: chosen = own reservation, unless already committed
  end
  Reserve -> PostgreSQL: UPDATE cargos SET destination_location_name = chosen,\nreserved_location_name = NULL, slot_decision_seq = seq + 1

  opt chosen was another cargo's reservation (swap)
    Reserve -> Slots: rank(layout, committed + other reservations + chosen)
    Slots --> Reserve: replacement slot | none
    Reserve -> PostgreSQL: UPDATE the displaced cargo's reserved_location_name
  end
  Reserve -> PostgreSQL: COMMIT (releases the zone lock)
  Reserve --> Loop: {slot, keptOwnReservation, displaced}

  opt not keptOwnReservation
    Loop -> Orders: reissue(task, vehicle, slot)
    Orders -> ACL: withdrawTransportOrder(old TO3)
    Orders -> ACL: createTransportOrder(new TO3 @ committed slot)
  end

  opt displaced is present
    Loop -> PostgreSQL: load the displaced cargo's DELIVERING task
    Loop -> Orders: reissue(victim task, victim vehicle, replacement slot)
    Orders -> ACL: withdrawTransportOrder + createTransportOrder
    Loop -> PostgreSQL: metadata.swapCount = swapCount + 1
  end
end

note over Loop, PostgreSQL
  Termination is structural: a commitment is irreversible and every swap
  ends in one, so a slot is stolen at most once and a cargo is displaced
  at most (fleet size − 1) times per trip. The intake capacity check keeps the cargo
  count at or below the reachable slot count, so a displaced cargo always has a slot left.
  Missing the tick at the gate is not an error — the commitment simply
  happens inside the zone and loses the right to swap.
end note

@enduml
